  "glossaryTerms": [
    {
      "slug": "cluster",
      "term": "Cluster",
      "definition": "Three trebles worked into the same chain-space, joined at the top. The basic building block of the granny square."
    },
    {
      "slug": "chain-space",
      "term": "Chain space",
      "definition": "The gap created by skipping a chain or chains. Corner chain-2 spaces hold the corner cluster pairs; side chain-1 spaces separate cluster pairs along the sides."
    },
    {
      "slug": "colour-change",
      "term": "Colour change",
      "definition": "In granny square work, the cleanest method is a fasten-off at the end of a round, then joining the new colour at the start of the next round with a slip stitch into a corner chain-space."
    }
  ],
  "techniqueSlugs": ["crochet-magic-ring", "crochet-working-in-the-round", "crochet-colour-change"],
  "criticalTechniques": ["crochet-magic-ring", "crochet-colour-change"],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The two-colour granny square uses a clean "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [{ "type": "glossaryTooltip", "attrs": { "termSlug": "colour-change" } }],
            "text": "colour-change"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at the end of round 2 to give a crisp contrasting border on a compact 10 cm motif. Colour A works rounds 1 and 2 — the central two rounds. Colour B picks up at round 3 and finishes at round 4. No yarn is carried and there are no floats: each colour fastens off cleanly when it finishes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [{ "type": "glossaryTooltip", "attrs": { "termSlug": "cluster" } }],
            "text": "cluster"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " construction and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [{ "type": "glossaryTooltip", "attrs": { "termSlug": "chain-space" } }],
            "text": "chain-space"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " structure are identical to the single-colour four-round granny. The only difference is that you fasten off colour A after round 2 and join colour B at a corner ch-2 space before starting round 3. The tail ends of both colours sit on the wrong side and weave in easily along the back of the cluster rows."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "tone": "tip",
          "title": "Materials for one motif",
          "body": "About 3 g of colour A and 3 g of colour B in DK-weight cotton. A 4 mm crochet hook (UK 8, US G/6). Tapestry needle. Scissors. A blocking mat and pins if you plan to block."
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Gauge" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each finished four-round two-colour granny square measures 10 × 10 cm in DK-weight cotton with a 4 mm hook, after a light steam-block. Work a test motif in a single colour first if the two-colour version is your first granny square."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Stitches used" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "chain (ch) — UK and US shared." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "slip stitch (sl st) — UK and US shared." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "treble (tr) — UK; called double crochet (dc) in US patterns." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "magic ring (MR) — adjustable starting loop; no centre hole." }] }] }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Pattern" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked in the round, right side facing throughout. Ch 3 at the start of each round counts as the first treble of the first cluster. Do not turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 1 — Colour A" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "With colour A, form a magic ring. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Work 2 tr into the ring. *Ch 2, 3 tr into the ring*; repeat from * to * twice more. Ch 2, sl st to top of beg ch-3. Pull tail to close ring. (12 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 2 — Colour A" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st across next 2 tr and into first ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3. Into same sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. *Ch 1, into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr)*; repeat from * to * twice more. Ch 1, sl st to top of beg ch-3. Fasten off colour A. (24 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 4 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 3 — Colour B" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join colour B with a sl st into any ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Into same sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. Ch 1. *Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1. Into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr). Ch 1.* Repeat from * to * twice more. Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1. Sl st to top of beg ch-3. (36 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 8 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 4 — Colour B" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into first ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3. Into same sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. Ch 1. *[Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1.] twice. Into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr). Ch 1.* Repeat from * to * twice more. [Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1.] twice. Sl st to top of beg ch-3. Fasten off colour B. (48 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 12 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Chart" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The chart reads outward from the magic ring. Rounds 1 and 2 are in colour A; rounds 3 and 4 in colour B. The colour change at the start of round 3 is shown as a new join at the corner ch-2 space."
          }
        ]
      },
